// One input and one gain, and the gain IS the parameter: a panel showing 0 means silent, 1 means
// full, with no second number to read it through. Two of these driven in MIRROR are a crossfader —
// without the second port a crossfade needs, so each side stays an ordinary track with an ordinary
// output and the blend happens where they meet at the mixer.
//
// `plugin: {type: jsdsp}` says the sound comes from the `jsdsp.ts` beside this file.
plugin({ type: "jsdsp", name: "Fade" })
params({
  // 1 is full, which is what an unwired fade should be: dropped into a chain alone it changes nothing.
  Level: 1,
})
// A fader. Two of them mirrored make a crossfade; on its own it is simply this lane's level.
// (To say this on the GRAPH, wire this module into a node of `@studio/doc`.)
